From: kevinbrar2024 <kevinbrar2024@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:28:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Announce an 'A or B' additional cost only between branches
 that can be paid (CR 601.2b, CR 601.2h)

A Choice additional cost (Bitter Triumph's 'discard a card or pay 3 life',
Countersculpt's 'behold a Jace or pay {1}') was announced whenever its first
branch was payable, so the prompt offered a second branch the cast then
rejected. The announcement now judges both branches against the costs and
reductions already settled on the cast, a Defiler's answer included, and takes
the only payable branch as its answer to the prompt would be.

The scenario cast driver answers a cost's card selection from the scripted
card-choice queue and stops at a game the cost payment ended (CR 704.5a).

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
